    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6521A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act relating to permitting the Green-Wood\ncemetery to file a certificate of incorporation with the department of\nstate\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation would authorize the secretary of state to accept for\nfiling from The Green-Wood Cemetery an application for a certificate\nof amendment of certificate of incorporation pursuant to section 803\nof the not-for-profit corporation law.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 would authorize the secretary of state to accept for filing\nfrom The Green-Wood Cemetery, located in Brooklyn, an application for\na certificate of amendment. The filing would be required to within one\nyear of the effective date of this act.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Green-Wood Cemetery was created by a special act of the\nLegislature in 1838. The Legislature amended the Charter in 1839 and\n1846. The Green-Wood Cemetery has been not-for-profit state regulated\nentity.\n\nThis bill would allow The Green-Wood Cemetery to file a certificate of\namendment of their certificate of incorporation with the secretary of\nstate to comply with recent changes in the not-for-profit corporation\nlaw. This bill would also affirm the not-for-profit status of the\norganization.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
